E={4: 'A brother approaches, who rejected the Hermit, the brother now teary-eyed. He just looks with a pouting smile that holds back looming fears of all time, saying to him, “I love you, brother. I love you. I’m sorry, man. It’s okay.” His voice breaks constantly, his eyes drowning and red in weep.', 14: 'In a raging bite, the Hermit bites at the Lucifer, clawing, punching, and—', 28: '“Brother?” Hermit voices lowly, the skin stretched tight in red and blue bulges. Again, he muscles out, as needle through a stroke-stack, “Brother…? Brother…? I—don’t—”'}
